  <prompt>Implement D1: in `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` (:328), map the ADR-034 membership `byRole` result to a graded access level (owner→FullAccess, collaborator roles→Collaborate, designated view-only role→ViewOnly; default unmapped→Collaborate), replacing P1's flat `Collaborate` — so internal SPA users get per-project rights at parity with CIAM external users. Server-enforced.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. BFF auth engineer fluent in ADR-034 user-record membership, the shipped `CallerPrincipalResolver` workforce strategy, and access-level grading.</role>
  <goal>`WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` maps ADR-034 `byRole` membership to graded access levels via an explicit role→level table (owner→FullAccess Read+Create+Write+Delete; collaborator roles→Collaborate; view-only role→ViewOnly; default unmapped→Collaborate), replacing the flat `Collaborate`. `CallerPrincipal.GetAccessLevel/GetEffectiveRights` return the graded rights. Server enforces them (negative: view-only member Read-only; owner member can Delete). Unit + KEEP-path tests cover each level incl. negatives.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-12 D1 + spec Owner Clarification "Workforce within-project rights (D1)": grade by ADR-034 role→level (owner→FullAccess, collaborator→Collaborate, view-only→ViewOnly) for CIAM parity; role data already exists. FR-22 remaining work: implement D1 in F3/F5 via `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` mapping the ADR-034 `byRole` result to graded levels instead of flat `Collaborate` — teams-app-r1's named extension point. P1 keeps flat `Collaborate` (plumbing-first); this task lands the grading. Resolved question: mapping = membership role `owner` → FullAccess (Read+Create+Write+Delete); collaborator roles (assignedAttorney, member, …) → Collaborate; a designated view-only role → ViewOnly; default unmapped → Collaborate. Exact role→level table finalized here with the schema work.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs — `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` :328 is THE edit site (currently returns flat `Collaborate`); `CallerPrincipal` :66 exposes `GetAccessLevel`/`GetEffectiveRights`. Map byRole→level here.</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs — `IAccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeAsync` :45 produces the ADR-034 membership set (with role info) the grading maps over.</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/WorkforcePrincipalResolver.cs — `IWorkforcePrincipalResolver` :42 (resolve/deny workforce principal).</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md — the membership model + byRole semantics that define which roles exist.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>Task 024 (workforce-plane policy) authenticates the workforce principal this grading applies to. Reuses the shipped `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` / `IAccessibleRecordSetService` (teams-app-r1).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec-D1">The role→level map MUST be: owner→FullAccess (Read+Create+Write+Delete); collaborator roles→Collaborate; designated view-only role→ViewOnly; default unmapped→Collaborate. Replace the flat `Collaborate`. Scope: `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` grading only — do NOT change the CIAM strategy's grading.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Derive roles from the ADR-034 `byRole` membership result already produced by `IAccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeAsync`; do NOT introduce a new membership source. Scope: grading input.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-NFR06">The graded rights MUST be server-enforced — a view-only member cannot Write/Delete regardless of client flags; an owner member can Delete. Negative test required. Scope: enforcement of the graded level.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-NFR08">This changes Tier-2 record-scope grading ONLY; it does not touch Tier-1 module entitlement. Scope: Tier-2 grading.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Placement Justification in the PR (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); `dotnet publish -c Release` compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline (≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` before the PR (edits the shipped teams-app-r1 `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` — direct conflict surface).</constraint>
  </constraints>
