    <patterns>
      <pattern name="workforce-strategy-grading" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs">`WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` (:328) is the teams-app-r1 named extension point — replace the flat `Collaborate` with a byRole→level map; `CallerPrincipal.GetEffectiveRights` returns the graded rights.</pattern>
      <pattern name="accessible-record-set" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs">`ComposeAsync` (:45) supplies the ADR-034 byRole membership the grading consumes.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec FR-12 D1 + the resolved D1 mapping + ADR-034. Read `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` (:328) + `CallerPrincipal` (:66 GetAccessLevel/GetEffectiveRights) + `AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeAsync` (:45) to confirm where role info flows.</step>
    <step order="2">Enumerate the actual ADR-034 membership role values available from `ComposeAsync`'s byRole result (empirical — read the membership model). Finalize the role→level table: owner→FullAccess; collaborator roles (assignedAttorney, member, …)→Collaborate; the designated view-only role→ViewOnly; default unmapped→Collaborate. Document the finalized table in notes/.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the mapping in `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy`: for each accessible project, map its byRole to the graded level; populate `CallerPrincipal.ProjectAccess` so `GetAccessLevel`/`GetEffectiveRights` return graded rights (replacing flat `Collaborate`).</step>
    <step order="4">Verify enforcement points consume the graded level (endpoint/filter authorization uses `GetEffectiveRights`, not a hardcoded level) so server-side enforcement is real.</step>
    <step order="5">Add unit + KEEP-path tests (ADR-038): owner-role member → FullAccess (can Delete on that project); collaborator-role member → Collaborate; designated view-only-role member → ViewOnly (Read-only; cannot Write/Delete — negative, server-enforced); unmapped role → Collaborate (default); a member of one project gets NO rights on a project they're not a member of (negative).</step>
    <step order="6">Build + test: `dotnet build` + `dotnet test`. Run `dotnet publish -c Release` and record compressed size + delta.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `/conflict-check` (edits shipped teams-app-r1 file); write Placement Justification + publish-size delta into the PR/task notes.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the ADR-034 byRole result does NOT expose a role value that cleanly maps to the "designated view-only role" (i.e. view-only cannot be distinguished from collaborator in the membership data), STOP and confirm the view-only role identity with the owner (§6) before defaulting it to Collaborate — a silent default would grant write to intended read-only users.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish .NET</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs (WorkforcePrincipalStrategy byRole→level grading)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + KEEP-path tests for each graded level incl. view-only negative</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ (finalized role→level table)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce user with `owner` role on a project, when authorized, then they receive FullAccess (Read+Create+Write+Delete) and can Delete on that project.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce user with a collaborator role, when authorized, then they receive Collaborate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce user with the designated view-only role, when they attempt Write/Delete, then it is denied server-side (ViewOnly, Read-only — negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce user with an unmapped role, when authorized, then they receive Collaborate (default) — not FullAccess.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a workforce user, when they access a project they are not a member of, then they receive no rights (negative — grading applies only within membership).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `dotnet publish -c Release`, when measured, then compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline is reported and ≤60 MB; BFF suite passes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Brownfield: this REPLACES the flat `Collaborate` in the shipped `WorkforcePrincipalStrategy` (teams-app-r1's named extension point) — it is a modification of existing surface, not new surface (no justification block required). Enumerate real byRole values empirically before finalizing the table (§F.3 empirical-reproduction-first). Do NOT hardcode a level in endpoints — enforce via `GetEffectiveRights`. This is the exact file teams-app-r1 owns; /conflict-check is mandatory.</notes>
